{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q25323782","formula":"PN","hill":"NP","elements":["N","P"],"composition":{"N":1.0,"P":1.0},"names":{"en":"Phosphorus mononitride","ru":"Мононитрид фосфора"},"descriptions":{"en":"Phosphorus mononitride is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula PN. Containing only phosphorus and nitrogen, this material is classified as a binary nitride. From the Lewis structure perspective, it can be represented with a P-N triple bond with a lone pair on each atom. It is isoelectronic with N2, CO, P2, CS, NO+, CN− and SiO. The compound is highly unstable in standard conditions, tending to rapidly self polymerize.","ru":"Мононитрид фосфора — химическое соединение, состоящее из азота и фосфора с химической формулой PN. Состоит только из азота и фосфора, является бинарным нитридом. С точки зрения структуры Льюиса, он может быть представлен тройной связью P-N с неподеленной парой на каждом атоме. Он изоэлектронен с N2, CO, P2, CS, NO+, CN− и SiO. Соединение крайне нестабильно в стандартных условиях и имеет тенденцию к быстрой самополимеризации."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":117441,"mass":44.981,"charge":0,"smiles":"N#P","inchikey":"AOPJVJYWEDDOBI-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"azanylidynephosphane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"117441","atoms":2,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.693,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"P"},{"x":-0.693,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"N"}],"bonds":[[0,1,3]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q25323782","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phosphorus_mononitride","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9C%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B